les that can be reasonably accepted by all parties involved.</p><p>In summa=
ry, contractualism provides a robust ethical framework that emphasizes mutu=
al respect, individual moral status, and the importance of justifying actio=
ns to others. Its focus on interpersonal relationships and the rejection of=
